      {
        "id": 28331,
        "name": "AnachronismAxe",
        "username": "AnachronismAxe",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/anachronismaxe/{size}/2163_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-05-02T23:29:52.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;evandan55&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"evandan55\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I actually like Axe’s idea: maybe he’ll play where he picks one target, and just focuses all damage on that one hero, and when they die, he moves onto the next one. Then his flip mechanic might be something like “flip when a hero dies”. But I doubt both of those are likely. He’ll probably still have lots of attacks that do various things. It’d be weird for a villain to literally focus on one hero, basically ensuring that every game, someone will die. I mean, it could work, and would be cool, but I can’t see it actually happening.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Doesn’t mean that there wouldn’t be ways to redirect who his target is. Maybe a condition on his description card or one of his other cards. Something like “If the heroes deal X damage then they can choose his new target”. Or he flips when a hero gets below a certain threshold of their HP or something like that.</p>",
