      {
        "id": 28332,
        "name": "EvanDan55",
        "username": "EvanDan55",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/evandan55/{size}/2374_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-05-02T23:40:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;AnachronismAxe&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"AnachronismAxe\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Doesn’t mean that there wouldn’t be ways to redirect who his target is. Maybe a condition on his description card or one of his other cards. Something like “If the heroes deal X damage then they can choose his new target”. Or he flips when a hero gets below a certain threshold of their HP or something like that.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Good point. If that is the case, I can see a lot of arguments going down about who has to be the target. But hey, that would just make him more scary, because he’d be turning the players against each other <span class=\"bbcode-i\">in real life</span>. Devious!</p>\n<p>But my other guess would be that he’d do a good amount of damage to just a couple of heroes. Something like doing the two heroes with the highest HPs <span class=\"bbcode-b\">H</span> minus one damage. That’d just be one card though.</p>",
